# a list concatenated with a non-list via `+` -- CPython raises TypeError at
# run time; NilPy resolves types statically and catches it as a compile error
# instead of silently corrupting the result (bug-nilpy-list-plus-nonlist-
# silently-corrupts-instead-of-typeerror).
a = [1, 2, 3]
print(a + "x")
